<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanhadadeva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1311">1311</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kanhadadeva was the Chahamana (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a>) king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalore">Jalor</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> at the turn of the 14th century. He resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, whose armies took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siwana">Siwana</a> in 1308 and then besieged Jalor, capturing it in 1311; Kanhadadeva and his son Viramadeva were killed. His stand is celebrated in the 15th-century epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanhadade-prabandha">Kanhadade Prabandha</a>.</p></div>
